<p>
  ASCII is one type of character code, but 128 characters is not enough for today’s computers, which can represent Chinese, Hindi, and scripts from many other languages. Today’s computers use a system called Unicode, which has more than 100,000 different characters and covers more than 100 different scripts (languages). 
</p>

